<b>Click</b>

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:01.380
<b>Click</b>

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.880
Well, now you've gained some experience,

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.250
<b>Click</b>

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.250
<b>Click</b>

00:01:01.880 --> 00:01:02.250
<b>Click</b>

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:06.000
but you can't use any of the techniques
I just showed you because

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.880
your opponents typically won't use martial arts to attack.

00:01:07.880 --> 00:01:09.040
Go ahead and forget it all.

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:09.920
Curse you!

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:25.080
The excitement has just begun!

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:32.670
I have a feeling that a miracle will occur

00:01:32.670 --> 00:01:39.920
A novice's skill is enough. Now, let's go!

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:42.880
It's all or nothing. We can go anywhere

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:47.630
Let me hear more even the sound of the core

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:52.420
If you and I put our hands together, there is nothing to fear

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.920
When I'm at a loss what to do,

00:01:55.420 --> 00:02:01.040
I'll remember that you are here for me

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:08.540
You and I look up at the same sky

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:12.920
We smile at each other and overcome hardship, too

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:18.170
Doing our best for someone

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:20.750
Isn't bad, too,

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:25.330
We are side by side again today

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.580
The excitement has just begun

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.040
<b>SPARKS FLY?!</b>

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.040
<b>LIGHT AND DARK GO ON A JOINT EXCURSION!</b>

00:02:45.290 --> 00:02:48.790
I made plans to visit the zoo with Momo and Mikan.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:52.380
I wanna eat a lunch that you
spared no effort to make for me.

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:55.880
This is my big chance to show
just how dependable a Demon Girl can be!

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.960
I'm gonna make the greatest
and most sublime lunch in existence!

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.170
I'll do a practice run using
the ingredients we have in the house first.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.830
<b>SOME</b>

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.830
<b>HOURS</b>

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:13.830
<b>LATER</b>

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:22.290
What do you think? How does it look?

00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:24.460
Who are you talking to, Shamiko?

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.960
I think it's boring since the colors don't pop.

00:03:26.960 --> 00:03:30.330
If we're going out for a picnic,
then I want it to have more glitz and glam.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:34.040
I think the darker tones look nice.
Fitting for a demon, anyway.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:37.960
But I need to take the magical girls by surprise
by making something that packs a punch!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.710
Okay, try covering the whole thing
with seaweed to make it pitch-black,

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:43.130
then adding a healthy splash of ketchup
right in the middle!

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:46.210
<b>CURSED</b>

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.130
Demonic Lunch, garnished with gore.

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.080
<b>DEMONIC LUNCH</b>

00:03:43.710 --> 00:03:46.080
<b>~GARNISHED WITH GORE~</b>

00:03:46.210 --> 00:03:48.080
That's not the kind of surprise I meant!

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.330
Aw, poo...

00:03:49.540 --> 00:03:52.580
Gosh, Shamiko, the color of this lunch you made
reminds me of dead leaves...

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:55.460
I think I'm going to retract my offer
to become your vassal.

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:56.460
Whaaaaaaat?!

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:00.750
I just don't have enough experience making lunches.
This calls for a different approach!

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.580
I'll go ahead and put this lunch
that you made in the fridge, then.

00:04:04.580 --> 00:04:07.250
The dead leaf coloring makes it seem extra appetizing!

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.920
<b>CAFÉ</b>

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:10.920
<b>ASURA</b>

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.130
You want help making a box lunch?

00:04:10.330 --> 00:04:10.920
Yeah.

00:04:11.290 --> 00:04:15.380
Can you teach me how to make a lunch
that would leave a magical girl drooling?

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.630
I figured you two might know since you sold
those fancy box lunches the other day.

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.460
Ah, you mean the ones
from the shopping district festival?

00:04:19.460 --> 00:04:22.460
We've got box lunches for sale! Buy tasty box lunches here!

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:23.580
Yes, those ones!

00:04:23.750 --> 00:04:26.920
Well, that tickles me pink! I'll gladly teach you, hun!

00:04:27.290 --> 00:04:30.080
Alrighty, the first step to a good lunch
is picking your ingredients.

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:31.960
Are those leaves?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:37.250
From the right: one that paralyzes, one that causes
drowsiness, and one that heats the body up.

00:04:37.500 --> 00:04:40.210
Um, just so we're clear, I'm not trying to drug anybody!

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.710
<b>LEAF THAT</b>

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.710
<b>HEATS THE BODY</b>

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.710
<b>LEAF THAT</b>

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.710
<b>CAUSES DROWSINESS</b>

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.710
<b>LEAF THAT</b>

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.710
<b>PARALYZES</b>

00:04:40.210 --> 00:04:43.710
<b>100% ORGANIC</b>

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.670
Ain't nothing to worry about, they're totally organic!

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:46.290
So, you wanna make a colorful lunch, huh?

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:49.000
Personally, I think a brown shade is just fine.

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:52.330
Because what matters most
are the vibes that you put into it.

00:04:52.330 --> 00:04:53.710
What do you mean?

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:58.330
Just picture your friends happily chowing down
on your food and then let your hands do the work.

00:04:58.330 --> 00:05:01.130
Is it just me or are your hands glowing?!
Is everything okay?!

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.000
Here. For you, bossman!

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:03.880
Uh, no thanks.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:05.960
Eat up!

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:09.580
This tasty morsel is filled with my positive vibes...

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:11.750
Can't you see?

00:05:12.630 --> 00:05:13.710
Eat up!

00:05:15.880 --> 00:05:21.330
Amazing, Lico. There are so many rainbow leaves
flying through the air right now...

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.880
Ain't it just wonderful?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.960
That's a big nope! Please teach me something else!

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>GLOWING RICEBALL</b>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>RICE:     A GOOD AMOUNT</b>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>SALT:          TO TASTE</b>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>MAKES YOU HALLUCINATE</b>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>RAINBOW LEAVES</b>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>SEAWEED:      DAMP</b>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>VIBES:         PLENTIFUL</b>

00:05:24.960 --> 00:05:33.080
<b>*Effectiveness will vary by person</b>

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:26.710
Your taste buds won't believe how

00:05:26.710 --> 00:05:28.960
mind-blowingly delicious these Huli jing riceballs are!

00:05:28.960 --> 00:05:30.710
Absolutely not available for purchase!

00:05:30.920 --> 00:05:32.540
It's chow time!

00:05:33.130 --> 00:05:34.670
Listen, Yuko.

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:38.130
You gotta make sure that the flavors and colors
of your side dishes don't overlap.

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:40.960
Separate 'em like: sweet, sour, and salty.

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.580
Uh-huh. I got it.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:50.420
Then for colors: red, yellow, green, black, and white are
the best ones to use to make something look really tasty.

00:05:45.080 --> 00:05:52.380
Rainbow cellophane! Marmalade sky! I am the egg man.

00:05:50.420 --> 00:05:52.380
C'mon, let's give it a try!

00:05:52.540 --> 00:05:54.710
You know how to make just about anything, huh, Lico?

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:57.130
Well, I've spent a long time moseying
from one place to the next.

00:05:57.330 --> 00:05:59.630
So I learned how to make food from all over the world.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.080
Which is nice and all, but no matter where I seem to go...

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:07.210
...for some cockamamie reason I always end up
getting chased around and then forced to quit.

00:06:07.210 --> 00:06:09.460
Come now, Lico! The reason for that should be obvious!

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:12.710
It's because you do crazy things like
giving your employer psychedelic hallucinations!

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:17.500
Aw. But I just wanted to show you something pretty,
since I adore you so much, boss.

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:18.420
You're forgiven.

00:06:18.420 --> 00:06:19.460
So he's okay with it...

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:23.540
There were also a lot of times
when I had to quit after a priestess found me.

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:27.630
I took an interest in cooking pretty much right after
I became able to disguise myself as human.

00:06:27.630 --> 00:06:37.960
<b>Soy Sauce</b>

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:33.630
I snuck my way into a number of kitchens
and always cooked dishes with great love and care.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:37.960
<b>Mirin</b>

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:37.960
<b>Sake</b>

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:37.960
<b>Garlic</b>

00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:37.960
<b>Ginger</b>

00:06:33.880 --> 00:06:38.290
But back when I was a cub, I would put
a teeny-weeny bit too many positive vibes in my food.

00:06:35.250 --> 00:06:37.960
<b>Salt</b>

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:37.960
<b>Pepper</b>

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:43.960
<b>CLOSED</b>

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:39.040
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:43.960
Give us food! Give us food! Give us food! Give us food!

00:06:38.420 --> 00:06:39.380
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:38.630 --> 00:06:42.080
Which sorta caused a teeny-weeny problem
with crowds banging at the doors.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:39.880
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:40.460
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:41.000
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.500
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:42.380
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:42.960
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.960
That sounds like more than a teeny-weeny problem!

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.250
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:43.250 --> 00:06:43.960
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:43.750 --> 00:06:43.960
<b>Give us food!</b>

00:06:43.960 --> 00:06:49.960
So, I kept having to move around after the local priestess
caught on to me and eventually ended up here.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.830
Sounds like an ordeal.

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:54.210
Now I know better.

00:06:54.210 --> 00:06:58.330
The best kind of smile that my food can put
on a customer's face is a completely natural one.

00:06:58.630 --> 00:07:02.330
Being able to cook in this city
without any fuss is like a dream come true.

00:07:02.630 --> 00:07:06.250
And it's all thanks to Lady Sakura
and the bossman here for taking me in.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:07.380
Aw, Lico...

00:07:07.710 --> 00:07:13.040
I get to eat three meals and nap on the job, plus I don't
have to come out of my den when I don't feel like it,

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:15.880
and lately I haven't had to interact
with the customers at all.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:17.210
It's Heaven.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:18.250
Uh, Lico?

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:22.420
<b>Marinate for 20 Minutes</b>

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:22.420
Anyhoo, it seems like most priestesses
don't care two hoots about us these days.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:24.540
But you should still be careful out there, hun.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:30.250
You know, not every Magical Girl out there
is the easy-going type like I am!

00:07:30.250 --> 00:07:31.880
Some of them have absolutely no mercy!

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:36.880
In the worst-case scenario, you, your family, and all
the Demons that live here might end up being hunted.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:38.130
I want you to protect them and yourself.

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:41.000
What even are Magical Girls, anyway?

00:07:41.540 --> 00:07:44.040
Who asked them to fight in the first place?

00:07:44.040 --> 00:07:47.210
Do they get some kind of reward for defeating demons?

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:52.380
Magical Girls are ordinary humans who fight after
they forge a pact with beings from the Light Clan.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:53.580
Or so I hear.

00:07:53.710 --> 00:07:54.830
The time hath come!

00:07:53.710 --> 00:08:01.000
<b>FAMILIARS OF THE LIGHT CLAN</b>

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:57.790
From what I understand, the girls who get contracted

00:07:56.460 --> 00:07:57.380
Wassup?!

00:07:57.790 --> 00:08:01.000
are chosen by familiars of the light clan that have
possessed animal bodies.

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:02.040
Gulp...

00:08:01.130 --> 00:08:01.920
<b>Gulp...</b>

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:04.500
And who exactly is the "Light Clan"?

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:06.170
I have no idea.
I got no clue.<b></b>

00:08:08.170 --> 00:08:12.420
We haven't had much of an opportunity for peaceful talks
with anybody from the magical girl side, you know.

00:08:12.420 --> 00:08:15.380
You should ask Lady Momo if you want to learn more.

00:08:15.380 --> 00:08:21.790
<b>HAMMER</b>

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:21.420
But in terms of a reward, I know that whenever a magical
girl succeeds in weakening and incapacitating us,

00:08:21.420 --> 00:08:25.000
they receive some sort of
"vanquishment token" from their familiar.

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.460
And it seems they are rewarded
after collecting a number of those.

00:08:28.460 --> 00:08:29.500
A token...

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:33.750
The more of those tokens that they collect,
the grander the wish they can have granted.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:38.380
They get a wish granted?!
That sounds like a really good deal!

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:42.040
You said it. In a matter of speaking,
we're like a walking jackpot to them.

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.500
But the majority of magical girls these days are friendly.

00:08:45.500 --> 00:08:48.670
You'll be fine as long as you avoid doing anything
to disrupt the peace in the neighborhood.

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:50.040
Hopefully.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:55.830
Despite how much they'd gain from defeating me,
Momo and Mikan have been protecting me instead...

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:57.290
<b>VICIOUS MIKAN</b>

00:08:57.710 --> 00:09:00.000
Nothing in my wardrobe is suitable for a picnic...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.080
But I feel pretty weird wearing yours.
Momowampus...<b></b>

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:01.960
<b>Momowampus...</b>

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.500
Given your physique, I think you'd be better off
wearing a simple, black t-shirt or something.

00:09:08.380 --> 00:09:11.880
O-oh my gosh, I'm gonna have to make
an ultra yummy lunch to try and return the favor!

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:14.330
It has to be something to put a smile on their faces!

00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.960
That's the spirit!

00:09:16.420 --> 00:09:20.040
Use this mushroom that'll make it
so they can't stop laughing!

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:21.460
No way, José!

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:26.750
The meat's all seasoned, so let's get to cookin'.

00:09:27.250 --> 00:09:31.290
We've only got one wok that's prepped for use right now,
so I'll show you how it's done.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:34.580
Oh, that's not a problem. I think I can make another wok!

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:35.830
Say what?

00:09:35.960 --> 00:09:38.290
Well, there's this rod that I inherited from my father.

00:09:38.830 --> 00:09:40.830
And I can transform it into pretty much anything!

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:45.630
This is a perfectly seasoned and refined wok...
It's got a film of oil covering the whole thing.

00:09:45.790 --> 00:09:50.000
What on Earth? Nothing should be able to transform like
that without totally disregarding the laws of nature!

00:09:50.170 --> 00:09:52.630
I don't really get how it works, but it sure is convenient.

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:55.500
That seems like a huge understatement
considering what it can do!

00:09:55.500 --> 00:09:57.750
It's a lifesaver whenever I forget to bring a pen!

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:00.710
So, it can just transform without any restrictions?

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:04.380
As long as it's something I can imagine
as being stick-like in my head,

00:10:04.380 --> 00:10:06.330
then it can become pretty much whatever I want.

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:08.040
Will you let me have it?

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:09.500
Uh, I don't think so...

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:12.170
Lico, dear, you really need to fix
those bad habits of yours.

00:10:12.540 --> 00:10:14.380
You can dive into people's dreams, right?

00:10:14.580 --> 00:10:16.580
Pretty much anybody who's asleep, yeah.

00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:21.290
I hope you don't feel your talents are wasted working
in this podunk café. You're not going to quit on us, right?!

00:10:21.290 --> 00:10:23.790
Uh, yeah. I'd very much like to keep working here.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:27.080
You know, there is a good possibility...

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:31.630
...that you could save a lot of people
if you put your mind to it.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:32.330
Huh?

00:10:32.330 --> 00:10:36.290
However, for her to have so much raw potential
at such a young age

00:10:36.460 --> 00:10:42.130
means that her powers could mature considerably
in either a good way or a bad way as she gets older.

00:10:42.580 --> 00:10:46.290
I just hope that no callous magical girls
set their sights on her.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:46.290
Focus, hun.

00:10:47.250 --> 00:10:49.290
The fried chicken was burnt black in an instant!

00:10:49.290 --> 00:10:51.710
It's because you let the oil get too hot.

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:55.420
I guess even your almighty rod
still needs temperature control.

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.750
I'm sure the potential is there, but... yeah.

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:06.130
<b>YOU CAN CALL</b>

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:06.130
<b>YOURSELF A PRO!</b>

00:10:59.210 --> 00:11:06.130
<b>WOK PRE-SEASONED WITH OIL</b>

00:10:59.790 --> 00:11:03.750
The oil film that coats this pan has been carefully
produced to mimic those belonging to master chefs!

00:11:03.920 --> 00:11:06.000
Enjoy the pleasure of being a pro in your very own home!

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:06.540
<b>SIMPLE</b>

00:11:06.130 --> 00:11:06.540
<b>BLACK T-SHIRT</b>

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:10.330
Mikan gave me all that advice about clothes, but...
I honestly don't get it.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:12.630
<b>SIMPLE                 SIMPLE</b>

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:12.630
<b> BLACK T-SHIRT      WHITE T-SHIRT</b>

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.630
What does she mean by "a simple black t-shirt"?

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:15.960
<b>SIMPLE BLACK T-SHIRT</b>

00:11:15.960 --> 00:11:24.170
<b>SIMPLE BLACK T-SHIRT</b>

00:11:16.130 --> 00:11:17.170
Heck yeah!

00:11:17.170 --> 00:11:19.420
Excuse me! Can I get this in an L size?

00:11:19.630 --> 00:11:24.170
Don't give up, Magical Girl! Get through the summer
with a simple and coordinated wardrobe.

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:26.460
Very simple!

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:26.540
<b>SIMPLE BLACK T-SHIRT</b>

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.960
My sample side dishes are finished!

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.170
Good on ya!

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.920
I know! Why don't you use the lacquer lunch
boxes we have in the shop?

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:37.750
You went through so much to cook that lunch,
you might as well make it look extra pretty!

00:11:37.750 --> 00:11:39.420
Wow, thank you!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:43.580
Except there's one little problem.
This box was made to fit enough food for 4 or 5 people.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:48.290
This picnic is just for you and 2 magical girls, right?
You're gonna end up with some leftovers.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:47.790
<b>UHHHHH...</b>

00:11:49.630 --> 00:11:50.710
Here's an idea!

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.290
<b>THE NEXT DAY</b>

00:11:51.330 --> 00:11:53.290
<b>THE PARK WHERE YOU CAN FIND LOTS OF CATS</b>

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.130
There are so many cats here!

00:11:57.750 --> 00:12:00.040
Yeah, this is the park where you can find lots of cats.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:02.540
So, you settled on wearing that outfit, huh?

00:12:02.670 --> 00:12:06.670
There was a black t-shirt that seemed perfect for me.
But they didn't have it in my size.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.500
Thanks for letting me borrow these.

00:12:09.710 --> 00:12:12.500
You're welcome! But c'mon, why so grumpy?

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:16.830
I don't mean to sound ungrateful,
but I just don't think this is a good look for me.

00:12:16.830 --> 00:12:19.630
Momo! Mikan! Good morning!

00:12:19.630 --> 00:12:20.380
Shamiko!

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:22.460
Hey, Momo! Nice to see you!

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:24.670
Uh, yeah, hello there...

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:25.290
What?

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:26.500
You're heavy!

00:12:25.460 --> 00:12:27.000
<b>You're heavy!</b>

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:28.130
I am so sorry.

00:12:28.380 --> 00:12:30.670
I was utterly powerless to stop Lico.

00:12:30.670 --> 00:12:35.170
I've never been to a zoo before!
Let's all have a good time!

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:36.210
Oh wow!

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:39.420
You're looking cuter than a button today, hun!

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.420
Why? What's the occasion?

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:43.380
Uh, right. But I'm going to get changed now.

00:12:44.250 --> 00:12:48.420
Don't give up, Shamiko!
The day for your get-together at the zoo has come!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:04.460
<b>Tama Zoological Park</b>

00:13:01.380 --> 00:13:04.250
Tama Zoological Park!

00:13:05.210 --> 00:13:07.540
Now it's time for an exciting trip to the zoo!

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:09.880
Let's have a blast today, you guys!

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:12.920
All of us? Are you sure it's okay that we tag along?

00:13:10.210 --> 00:13:16.330
<b>Ticket</b>

00:13:13.040 --> 00:13:16.290
Of course! It says up to 5 people
can get in with this ticket.

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:23.210
<b>SHUDDER</b>

00:13:16.330 --> 00:13:23.210
<b>SHUDDER</b>

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:23.210
<b>SHUDDER</b>

00:13:16.340 --> 00:13:23.210
<b>SHUDDER</b>

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:19.460
It's not the number of us that I'm worried about, Yuko!

00:13:19.540 --> 00:13:23.210
Let's just say... it feels like an immense pressure
from nearby is about to squish me flat!

00:13:23.210 --> 00:13:24.880
What did you come for?

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:28.330
Today was supposed to be a fun day at the zoo.

00:13:28.460 --> 00:13:32.670
If you must know, we came here to help you
out of the goodness of our hearts.

00:13:32.670 --> 00:13:35.920
Shucks, Momo. It hurts to see you
get so steamed up about this.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.580
You even ditched that cute outfit you were wearing.

00:13:38.580 --> 00:13:44.210
<b>THE DAM IN MOMO'S HEART</b>

00:13:38.830 --> 00:13:39.920
Cut to the chase.

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:44.210
<b>Translation: Please explain yourself quickly</b>

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:44.210
<b>before the dam in my heart gets full enough to burst.</b>

00:13:40.040 --> 00:13:44.130
Please explain yourself quickly
before the dam in my heart gets full enough to burst.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:48.830
Well, we heard that you like animals!
And guess what? We're cute animals, too!

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:51.960
So, we figured that tagging along with you
would make today even more fun!

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:53.710
<b>AIN'T I</b>

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:53.580
Ain't I generous?

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:53.710
<b>GENEROUS?</b>

00:13:53.710 --> 00:13:54.750
How about that.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:58.170
<b>Translation: I get the feeling I won't be able to make</b>

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:58.170
<b>any sense of this, so I'm going to quit asking.</b>

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:57.380
I get the feeling I won't be able to make
any sense of this, so I'm going to quit asking.

00:13:58.290 --> 00:13:59.500
Don't be silly, Lico.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:02.880
You know that we came here for something
far more important. The magical girl here needs...

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:04.080
Yargh!

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:05.380
Boss!

00:14:05.380 --> 00:14:07.580
My back is still on the mend...

00:14:07.710 --> 00:14:08.710
<b>Ahaha!</b>

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:13.420
My apologies for being so fragile.
Just leave me behind and go enjoy the zoo...

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.580
Sounds good.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:17.580
We'll just have Lico take you back home right now.

00:14:17.580 --> 00:14:18.960
We can't do that!

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.460
Let me carry your bags!

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:21.880
Huh? You're letting them stay?

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:23.460
This is supposed to be a group outing!

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:25.710
Pain, pain, go away!

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:26.880
<b>PAIN</b>

00:14:25.790 --> 00:14:28.420
Whoa! Something did fly away!

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:29.920
Are you all right?
Chill~ Chill~<b></b>

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:29.960
<b>Chill~</b>

00:14:28.420 --> 00:14:29.960
<b>Chill~</b>

00:14:30.040 --> 00:14:33.630
I'm feeling better.
The cooling pad is working, so thank you.

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:41.460
<b>Benefits to Being a Bipedal Creature</b>

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:41.460
<b>-Can hold tools</b>

00:14:33.630 --> 00:14:41.460
<b>-Can support a large brain</b>

00:14:34.130 --> 00:14:37.040
My species is actually quadrupedal by nature, you see.

00:14:37.040 --> 00:14:41.460
So I often suffer from back pain
because I force myself to stand on two legs instead.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:43.290
Oh no, that's awful!

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:46.380
It's a living hell. But, that being said...

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:50.790
I have no other choice but to walk on two legs
if I want to keep a low profile when living among humans.

00:14:50.790 --> 00:14:54.750
I imagine that a tapir walking on two legs would actually
draw a ridiculous amount of attention to itself,

00:14:54.750 --> 00:14:56.420
but let's not sweat the small stuff.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:14:57.330
<b>That's rough</b>

00:14:56.580 --> 00:14:57.540
That's rough.

00:14:57.920 --> 00:15:00.080
I'm glad you made it back on your feet.

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.130
Thank you. Sorry for the trouble.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:05.080
Momo!

00:15:06.380 --> 00:15:09.670
Are you sure you didn't just want to do this
alone with Shamiko?

00:15:09.670 --> 00:15:10.420
Huh?

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:14.380
No! I think going with a big group
is the best way to enjoy the zoo!

00:15:15.130 --> 00:15:18.170
But the problem is I basically assaulted
their café the first time we met,

00:15:18.170 --> 00:15:21.130
and I get the impression that Lico
doesn't enjoy my company very much.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:27.170
That couldn't be further from the truth, hun!
You're a little cutie-patootie in my eyes!

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:27.750
Huh?

00:15:28.130 --> 00:15:29.500
She's got an acute sense of hearing!

00:15:30.130 --> 00:15:32.330
Several times stronger than any human!

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:40.380
<b>THE MOUSE HOUSE</b>

00:15:32.710 --> 00:15:34.420
Anyhoo, let's go enjoy ourselves!

00:15:34.580 --> 00:15:39.420
We brought a really big lunch, so everybody's
gotta get in some steps to empty their bellies!

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:40.330
Okay!

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:44.080
Did you know that baby Malayan tapirs
have a very intricate camouflage on their fur?

00:15:44.080 --> 00:15:46.880
Wow, you're right!
They look totally different from the adults!

00:15:48.960 --> 00:15:50.880
So, are the itty-bitty animals your favorite?

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:51.830
I guess.

00:15:51.830 --> 00:15:53.330
Same here!

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:57.210
They cook real fast, which makes 'em good
boiled, baked, or even fried.

00:15:57.210 --> 00:15:58.630
I don't think we're on the same page here.

00:15:58.630 --> 00:16:07.580
Giraffe! Giraffe! Giraffe! Giraffe! Giraffe! Giraffe! Giraffe!

00:16:01.130 --> 00:16:04.130
You can tell that its summer vacation
from all the big crowds out today!

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:04.960
Yeah.

00:16:05.290 --> 00:16:07.080
What's that group over there looking at?

00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:07.580
Huh?

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:09.170
Boss?!

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:12.790
Oh, I'm not part of the petting zoo area.
But you're still welcome to pet me.

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:14.460
This tapir is so adorable!

00:16:14.460 --> 00:16:17.580
Wait. I think I remember this tapir from somewhere...

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:21.750
Oh, you're a regular at the café.
It's me! The owner of Asura.

00:16:22.460 --> 00:16:24.170
I wanna pet it!

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:30.170
<b>DOG</b>

00:16:25.960 --> 00:16:30.170
<b>STAYING AT HOME FOR TODAY</b>

00:16:27.080 --> 00:16:30.170
We'll go for a nice walk once I get back. Okay, boy?

00:16:30.380 --> 00:16:32.830
We offer pictures for 1,800 yen, folks!

00:16:30.830 --> 00:16:32.830
I wanna pet it!

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:35.170
Stop, Lico! None of your greedy little schemes!

00:16:35.750 --> 00:16:37.710
We heard one of the tapirs escaped!

00:16:37.960 --> 00:16:39.830
Oh, I'm just a tapir visiting from abroad.

00:16:40.080 --> 00:16:41.420
A tapir visiting a zoo...

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.670
Well, guess we don't have to catch a tapir
that's from somewhere else.

00:16:43.670 --> 00:16:46.130
<b>THE OWNER OF CAFÉ ASURA: SHIROSAWA</b>

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:45.960
I'm a good guy tapir!

00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:49.250
I'm so sorry for budging in on your girls' day out...

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:50.330
It's no problem.

00:16:50.630 --> 00:16:51.790
Oh, that reminds me.

00:16:51.960 --> 00:16:54.960
What was the important thing
you were trying to explain earlier?

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:58.880
Don't be silly, Lico. You know that we came here
for something far more important.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:01.500
The magical girl here needs... yargh!

00:17:01.500 --> 00:17:02.500
Ah, of course.

00:17:02.500 --> 00:17:05.580
We animals have more sensory organs
than you humans do,

00:17:05.580 --> 00:17:09.130
so sometimes we pick up
on strange things that you can't.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:11.750
And for that reason, there's something
concerning us about Lady Momo...

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:14.170
What is it?

00:17:15.880 --> 00:17:16.630
Momo!

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:19.920
I've been looking all over for you!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:23.000
Sorry. I got so distracted by the view here
that I fell behind.

00:17:23.500 --> 00:17:24.710
Are the others waiting for us?

00:17:24.710 --> 00:17:25.630
Actually...

00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:28.790
Everybody ended up having to go home all of a sudden.

00:17:28.920 --> 00:17:29.540
Huh?

00:17:30.130 --> 00:17:31.960
I gotta go home and water my potted mikan plants.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:34.920
Uh oh! I think I left the heat on the tempura oil!

00:17:34.920 --> 00:17:37.130
Ugh! I'm having one of my chronic fits of drowsiness!

00:17:37.330 --> 00:17:37.920
So...

00:17:37.920 --> 00:17:38.500
What the heck?

00:17:38.880 --> 00:17:41.460
And after all the trouble
I went through to make this big lunch!

00:17:41.750 --> 00:17:43.540
I hope they didn't leave for my sake...

00:17:43.710 --> 00:17:46.580
I'm sorry. Our fun little picnic
turned into such a huge mess.

00:17:46.580 --> 00:17:50.750
Oh, that's okay. To be honest,
I was kind of enjoying all the craziness.

00:17:51.080 --> 00:17:52.040
I'm glad to hear that.

00:17:52.290 --> 00:17:54.960
This seems like a good time for a break. Let's eat!

00:17:55.710 --> 00:17:56.380
Okay.

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.250
<b>SAKURA PLAZA</b>

00:17:57.000 --> 00:17:59.250
<b>A GREAT PLACE FOR A PICNIC</b>

00:18:00.830 --> 00:18:04.460
So, hey, I really want to get closer with you.
I'm glad we made the time to hang out.

00:18:04.710 --> 00:18:06.580
Now we finally have a chance to just talk.

00:18:07.040 --> 00:18:08.880
So, why did you become a magical girl, Momo?

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:11.670
<b>PRESS</b>

00:18:09.040 --> 00:18:11.670
<b>PRESS</b>

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:14.920
What do you want to be in the future?
What's your weakness? Are there any foods you hate?!

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:13.670
<b>PRESS</b>

00:18:11.670 --> 00:18:13.670
<b>PRESS</b>

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:16.790
<b>PRESS</b>

00:18:13.670 --> 00:18:16.790
<b>PRESS</b>

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:16.790
That's a pretty intense barrage of questions...

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:20.130
You know... I really love this city!

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:23.830
And since we're working together to protect it,
I want to know all about you!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.670
I feel exactly the same.

00:18:28.880 --> 00:18:29.460
But...

00:18:29.210 --> 00:18:29.920
<b>GRIP</b>

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.000
Huh?

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.630
Using dirty tricks like this... is a big no-no!

00:18:34.250 --> 00:18:35.960
Fresh Peach Outer Reap!

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.630
Aw, phooey!

00:18:38.630 --> 00:18:40.750
Why couldn't you just play along?

00:18:40.750 --> 00:18:43.130
I knew you'd pull something like this, Lico!

00:18:43.330 --> 00:18:46.830
So, I take it that you were trying to trick me
into eating these leaves, huh?

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:48.290
How'd you figure it out?

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:54.250
Your tone, gestures, level of eye contact, rhythm of
breath, tail movement, excess core strength, and so on.

00:18:54.250 --> 00:18:55.250
All of it was way off!

00:18:55.380 --> 00:18:57.210
Whoa... you can't be for real...

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:58.460
And most importantly...

00:18:58.920 --> 00:19:01.830
...there's no way Shamiko could ever be
that straightforward with me.

00:19:01.830 --> 00:19:05.330
Now I get it. That's really good to know.

00:19:05.330 --> 00:19:08.380
Lico! Lady Momo! Where have you been?!

00:19:08.830 --> 00:19:11.920
I blew it, boss! The switcheroo was a big failure!

00:19:11.920 --> 00:19:13.880
GROVEEEEL!

00:19:15.040 --> 00:19:18.460
I'm so sorry, I should have known better
than to let Lico out of my sight!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:20.580
Wow! It's a tapir!

00:19:18.460 --> 00:19:22.420
P-please pick yourself up. There are children watching.

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:27.170
If you want Lady Momo to take a dose of your medicine,
then you need to be upfront and ask her!

00:19:27.500 --> 00:19:28.210
Medicine?

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:30.330
Well, it's about your magic power.

00:19:30.670 --> 00:19:33.630
It's been a teeny-bit unstable recently.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:36.670
That's why I wanted you
to eat some of my medicinal cuisine.

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:39.080
It's really effective in curing unstable qi!

00:19:39.380 --> 00:19:41.580
These raw leaves are "medicinal cuisine"...?

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:45.210
I thought you might enjoy chowing down
on it more if I tricked you into it.

00:19:45.750 --> 00:19:50.080
I understand that you all used some extreme measures
when Lady Momo gave herself to the darkness.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:53.500
Swallowing strange elixirs
and forcibly changing her class.

00:19:53.830 --> 00:19:56.580
That's likely what caused her core
to become so unstable.

00:19:56.750 --> 00:20:00.750
It's bad for your body and mind
if you let your qi stay bent out of shape like that.

00:20:00.750 --> 00:20:03.790
But we knew you'd be too suspicious to trust us.

00:20:04.080 --> 00:20:07.580
Let me get this straight, you put on this whole ruse
just to try and get me to take medicine?

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:10.170
Lico is kind at heart and generally acts in good faith.

00:20:10.420 --> 00:20:13.210
But I also did it partly because watching
a priestess chew on grass that I tricked her into eating

00:20:13.210 --> 00:20:15.290
makes me laugh pretty hard.

00:20:15.290 --> 00:20:16.500
You need to shut up, Lico.

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:20.580
F-forget about that and let's all
patch things up over a nice lunch!

00:20:20.710 --> 00:20:22.460
I cooked a ton of stuff.

00:20:22.750 --> 00:20:23.960
<b>COLD</b>

00:20:23.960 --> 00:20:34.630
<b>GLASS / CANS           PLASTICS</b>

00:20:24.210 --> 00:20:29.170
Despite all the trickery, I was being honest
when I said that I want to get closer with you.

00:20:29.380 --> 00:20:32.920
Well, I don't have a problem taking medicine,
so long as you explain the situation to me first.

00:20:33.170 --> 00:20:34.000
Really?

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:37.920
Boy, I didn't think a baby tiger could be that fluffy!

00:20:37.920 --> 00:20:41.920
Being able to pet something with fur
that silky soft must come only once in a lifetime!

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.830
Yeah, you said it!

00:20:44.170 --> 00:20:45.460
Once in a lifetime...?

00:20:45.460 --> 00:20:47.830
Okay! Here's 800 of 'em to eat before lunch!

00:20:47.830 --> 00:20:49.710
I guess we're just never going to be on the same page.

00:20:50.080 --> 00:20:52.290
But you said you would take the medicine!

00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:53.580
I have my limits!

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.670
The whole reason I came here was to eat LUNCH!

00:20:55.670 --> 00:20:57.000
No fighting!

00:20:57.000 --> 00:20:58.330
Speaking of which, Momo...

00:20:58.790 --> 00:21:01.210
You haven't forgotten about
the other reason you came today, right?

00:21:01.210 --> 00:21:03.170
<b>SHOCK...</b>

00:21:01.580 --> 00:21:04.920
Your special chance to hug a baby tiger
that came with our VIP tickets...

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:12.250
<b>THE VIP</b>

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:12.250
<b>PETTING ZOO AREA</b>

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:12.250
<b>CLOSED AT 2 PM TODAY</b>

00:21:10.830 --> 00:21:12.250
I totally forgot...

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:15.250
Have I mentioned how fluffy I am in my fox form?

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:16.420
You can hug me if you want.

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:17.080
<b>SNAP</b>

00:21:16.580 --> 00:21:17.580
No thank you!

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:23.790
Don't think this means you've won...
Don't think this means you've won...

00:21:23.960 --> 00:21:26.920
Don't think this means you've won....

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:27.250
Momo! I wanna hug her next!

00:21:27.250 --> 00:21:28.000
Fluffy...

00:21:28.000 --> 00:21:30.830
Momo! I also wanna have a turn after that!

00:21:30.830 --> 00:21:31.790
Fluffy...

00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:36.960
Don't give up, Shamiko! Gather around the dining table
and let bygones be bygones.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:42.380
Lico was so soft to the touch!

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:43.920
I hope we can hug her again.

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:48.710
Seems like everybody enjoyed their day out at the zoo.

00:21:48.920 --> 00:21:49.830
Now then...

00:21:52.080 --> 00:21:55.830
I think it's about time for me
to start having some fun of my own...

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:01.500
Bwa? Wuzzat...?

00:22:01.500 --> 00:22:03.710
What have I been doing all this time?

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:06.420
Was I asleep? Have I been sleeping?

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:10.250
I think Shamiko said they were going
to visit the zoo or something...

00:22:10.250 --> 00:22:13.250
But nobody's tried to talk with me at all today...

00:22:13.540 --> 00:22:17.250
Shamiko? Momo? Mikan?

00:22:18.630 --> 00:22:21.250
I really wanted to have more dialog...

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:26.000
<b>TO BE CONTINUED</b>

00:22:21.630 --> 00:22:25.670
Hey guys, it's Anri! I managed to finish
all of my summer homework!

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:46.710
We met again. It's drama?

00:22:46.710 --> 00:22:49.710
I'll go tell someone at once

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:52.630
As soon as possible

00:22:52.750 --> 00:22:55.250
Oh, even the post box says "Good morning"

00:22:55.250 --> 00:22:57.460
Even my tail is sharp

00:22:57.460 --> 00:23:01.290
If our usual members gather and jump over the white lines

00:23:01.290 --> 00:23:04.040
Today will start, too

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:07.830
A sudden mystery

00:23:07.960 --> 00:23:11.210
Makes me feel dizzy and at a loss

00:23:11.460 --> 00:23:15.710
But we will hold hands and go anywhere we want

00:23:19.080 --> 00:23:22.670
The city is turning and shining

00:23:22.790 --> 00:23:25.580
Around and around many times

00:23:25.580 --> 00:23:28.290
The night mixed with dreams

00:23:28.290 --> 00:23:31.170
Will make you blossom

00:23:31.290 --> 00:23:34.170
The tetragon that surrounds four sides

00:23:34.170 --> 00:23:37.040
Ah, a bouquet for our neighborhood

00:23:37.040 --> 00:23:40.000
Hey, now, just a little bit more

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:44.040
Show me the flowers secretly

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:47.710
Once more if I get greedy!

00:23:56.080 --> 00:24:11.000
<b>PREVIEW</b>

00:23:56.830 --> 00:24:00.000
Time sure flies when you're having fun with friends, huh?

00:24:00.540 --> 00:24:01.750
I still refuse to accept this.

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:03.210
What's bothering you, Momo?

00:24:03.210 --> 00:24:04.790
Shamiko! Did you need me? Here I am!

00:24:04.790 --> 00:24:07.250
I know a whole bunch of stuff that could be helpful!

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:11.000
<b>PITCH-BLACK FEELINGS!! DARKNESS PEACH RETURNS!!</b>

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:08.670
In fact, here's something interesting about Chiyoda...

00:24:08.670 --> 00:24:10.830
Ogura! This isn't the place to advance the plot!
